---
layout: "layouts/base.njk"
title: "Staff & shift transport"
description: "Daily staff transport for AM, PM and night shifts across Cape Town. Live tracking, boarding codes and invoices matched to trips. Route plan and quote in 2 working days."
permalink: "/staff-transport/"
---
<section class="page-hero dark">
  <div class="container hero-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Staff &amp; shift transport</p>
      <h1>Your team at work on time, <span class="hl">every shift.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">Daily transport for AM, PM and night shifts across Cape Town. We plan the routes, run the cars and give you a live view of every trip, so HR stops being the transport desk.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="#quote">Get a quote</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-light" href="#pricing">How pricing works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="photo ratio-16-10"><img src="/assets/img/photos/staff-hero.jpg" alt="Morning traffic on Loop Street, Cape Town" width="1400" height="875"></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" style="padding-bottom:0">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="proof">
      <div><strong>2024</strong><span>running staff routes since</span></div>
      <div><strong>380+</strong><span>trips a month</span></div>
      <div><strong>3 shifts</strong><span>AM, PM and night</span></div>
      <div><strong>Live</strong><span>every trip tracked, start to finish</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Who it's for</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Built for teams that don't work nine to five.</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div class="card"><h3>CBD offices</h3><p>Staff who start before taxis run or finish after dark.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Call centres &amp; BPO</h3><p>Rotating shifts, night shifts and changing headcount.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Hospitality groups</h3><p>Early kitchens, late closes, staff across several sites.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Professional services</h3><p>Safe late-night transport as a staff benefit.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">What's included</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">One service, two sides.</h2>
    <div class="split" style="align-items:start">
      <div>
        <p class="card-label">For your staff</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>Book the month in the CapeX rider app</li>
          <li>Swap days or cancel without calling anyone</li>
          <li>See the driver and car before pickup</li>
          <li>Credits balance and trip history</li>
          <li>Rate the driver after each trip</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="shots" style="margin-top:0">
        <figure class="shot"><div class="shot-phone"><img src="/assets/img/app/rider-book-month.webp" alt="Rider app: booking the month by shift on a calendar" width="640" height="1300" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption>Book the month by shift</figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="shot"><div class="shot-phone"><img src="/assets/img/app/rider-change-trip.webp" alt="Rider app: changing a trip, with options for not travelling, a different day, shift or address" width="640" height="1300" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption>Change a trip without calling anyone</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="split" style="align-items:center;margin-top:3rem">
      <div>
        <p class="card-label">For HR &amp; ops</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>Live trip tracking from pickup to drop-off</li>
          <li>Boarding records: who got in, when, with a code</li>
          <li>Invoices matched to trips that actually ran</li>
          <li>A monthly report on trips, no-shows and late pickups, plus anything else you need tracked</li>
          <li>One ops contact on every shift</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="shot">
        <div class="shot-browser"><img src="/assets/img/app/liveops-waiting.webp" alt="CapeX Live Ops: driver waiting at a pickup, wait time flagged to ops, car shown on a map" width="1600" height="511" loading="lazy"></div>
        <figcaption style="max-width:none">Live Ops flags a wait the moment it happens. Map data © Google.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="shot-note center">Real app screens. Names, addresses, plates and numbers changed for privacy.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section band-dark">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Driver standards</p>
    <h2>Rules built into the driver app, not a poster.</h2>
    <p class="lead">Drivers sign off the rules every day. Any exception is logged and flagged to our ops team.</p>
    <div class="steps steps-6" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
      <div class="step"><h3>Vetted drivers</h3><p>Every driver holds a PrDP and is background-checked through Huru.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><h3>No third parties</h3><p>Only booked riders in the car.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><h3>Code every trip</h3><p>Each rider confirms with their 4-digit code.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><h3>Booked address only</h3><p>Drop-offs at the address on the trip.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><h3>GPS on</h3><p>App open for the whole trip.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><h3>3-minute wait</h3><p>Then we contact the rider and move on.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <figure class="shot"><div class="shot-phone"><img src="/assets/img/app/driver-arrived.webp" alt="Driver app: arrived at pickup with a 3-minute wait timer and call and WhatsApp buttons" width="640" height="1300" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption>The 3-minute wait, timed in the app</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="shot"><div class="shot-phone"><img src="/assets/img/app/driver-code.webp" alt="Driver app: entering the rider's 4-digit boarding code to confirm boarding" width="640" height="1300" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption>Every rider boards with their code</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="shot"><div class="shot-phone"><img src="/assets/img/app/driver-trip-complete.webp" alt="Driver app: trip complete summary with boarded, no-show and duration, and a boarding without a code reported to ops" width="640" height="1300" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption>Exceptions go straight to ops</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="pricing">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">How pricing works</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Quoted per rider, per month. Extras listed up front.</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div class="card"><h3>Monthly, in arrears</h3><p>Your rate is based on shifts, route and headcount. You're billed at month-end for the trips that ran.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Rules agreed up front</h3><p>Cancellations, address changes and extra drop-offs are set out in your quote. Nothing gets added later.</p></div>
</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Onboarding</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">From first call to first pickup</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><div class="step-num">01 · DISCOVER</div><p>Headcount, sites, shift times</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-num">02 · ASSESS</div><p>We map where your staff live</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-num">03 · PROPOSE</div><p>Route plan and quote in 2 working days</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-num">04 · IMPLEMENT</div><p>Staff get app invites and PIN codes</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-num">05 · REVIEW</div><p>Monthly check-in on the numbers</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container faq">
    <h2>Questions HR asks us</h2>
    <details><summary>What if a driver is late?</summary><p>Ops sees it live and contacts the rider. Lateness is tracked per driver and reported monthly.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do our staff have to download an app?</summary><p>It opens from a link on their phone and can be added to the home screen. No app store needed.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How many seats per car?</summary><p>Up to 4 riders per car, or 7 in our larger vehicles.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can headcount change month to month?</summary><p>Yes. Riders book each month, and we add cars through our partner fleet as you grow.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What does the data tell us?</summary><p>Every pickup time, delay and no-show is recorded. You get the numbers monthly, and we use them to plan routes and drivers.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section band-dark quote-band" id="quote">
  <div class="container split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Get a quote</p>
      <h2>Let's map your staff transport.</h2>
      <p>Tell us headcount, sites and shift times. We'll come back with a route plan and quote within 2 working days.</p>
      <p>Prefer to talk first? <a href="/contact/?service=call">Book a 15-minute discovery call</a>.</p>
      <ul class="contact-lines">
        <li>WhatsApp: <a href="https://wa.me/{{ contact.whatsapp }}" rel="noopener">{{ contact.whatsappDisplay }}</a></li>
        <li>Phone: <a href="tel:+27843772351">{{ contact.phone }}</a></li>
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:{{ contact.email }}">{{ contact.email }}</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      {% set formType = "contact" %}
      {% set service = "Staff transport quote" %}
      {% set askPhone = true %}
      {% set companyLabel = "Company" %}
      {% set extraFields = [
        { "label": "Your role", "half": true, "placeholder": "e.g. HR manager" },
        { "label": "Number of staff", "type": "number", "half": true, "required": true },
        { "label": "Shift times", "required": true, "placeholder": "e.g. 06:00–14:00 and 22:00–06:00, Mon–Sat" },
        { "label": "Site address(es)", "type": "textarea", "required": true }
      ] %}
      {% set messageLabel = "Anything else we should know" %}
      {% set submitLabel = "Send my request" %}
      {% set successText = "Thanks. We've got your request and will reply on WhatsApp or email, usually the same working day." %}
      {% include "partials/lead-form.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
